# Node/V8 flags for every ditto-hostd start. Each launch path puts them between
# node and dist/ditto-hostd.mjs: the systemd unit (@DITTO_HOSTD_NODE_FLAGS@,
# filled in by packaging/reference-image/install-session.sh), bin/ditto-hostd
# and the G1 runners (tests/g1/lib/common.sh g1_hostd_spec). hostd logs at
# start whether it got them. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Why (EX1-04, measured 2026-10-04 on a development machine, tests/g1/README.md):
# every plugin mount leaves short-lived Cordis contexts, closures and hidden
# classes behind. Heap snapshots show no growth in live objects, but with V8's
# defaults hostd's PSS kept climbing for hundreds of mount/unmount cycles:
#   --min/max-semi-space-size=4  fixed 4 MiB semi-spaces (8 MiB young
#                                generation). By default the young generation
#                                doubled under transaction churn and was not
#                                given back (new space 4 → 14 MiB after 100
#                                tasks disable/enable cycles, 27 MiB after 400).
#                                2 MiB promoted more garbage; 8 MiB took longer
#                                to touch.
#   --expose-gc                  lets hostd collect the old generation after a
#                                mount's disposers finished (src/reclaim.ts:
#                                coalesced, at most once a second). main.ts
#                                takes `gc` off the global object before any
#                                plugin loads.
--expose-gc --min-semi-space-size=4 --max-semi-space-size=4
